Z||000000||BN Boomer||02-28-2001||02:23 PM||||Gave the house a pretty good ride clear up here in Snohomish. Any one else feel it?||||reg||4
Z||000001||stimpy||02-28-2001||02:39 PM||||Been watching the live coverage on TV. Looks like y'all had a nice rumble. Having been in Mountain View, CA during the 7.2 of 1989, I can definately relate on what a wild ride that is! I got to watch 3 ft swells in the PAVEMENT! YEEE-HAW!<P>Hope it turns out that the only ones injuredis the insurance companies.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||02-28-2001||04:02 PM||||Yeah, we had to dive under our desks in Renton. Broke some windows, ceiling tiles, gas leaks, etc. Got the rest of the day off. Fiero survived intact, but at home, my cherished Motor Trend magazine with the Fiero GT got dumped in the toilet!||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||02-28-2001||05:01 PM||||Well, that was kind of neat.  Hope no one down south was injured or anything.  Would be nice to hear from Coconut about now.  ||||reg||10
Z||000004||LarryB||02-28-2001||05:17 PM||||Spoke to my counterpart in Seattle, he said this was the worst quake he's felt since he moved there in 1993.  Mostly broken glass and small stuff falling off of walls, nothing real serious, although everybody got out of the building fast.<P>We lost like 3000 dialup users in seconds, people probably either lost power or shut off their computers and ran outside, but we're seeing near-normal traffic again. That's a good sign, means that most people have power to their homes, many phones are working, and there aren't many widescale network outages.<P>Give thanks, it could have been a lot worse.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||02-28-2001||05:19 PM||||I was just watching it on TV. I was glad I didn't see any Fieros with bricks on them. I saw some other cars all dented up.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Raydar||02-28-2001||05:23 PM||||I was reading about this on CNN.com. Glad it wasn't any worse. Take care, out there. <P>Don't forget to duck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||MrPBody||02-28-2001||06:49 PM||||USGS bulletin:<BR> <A HREF="http://earthquake.usgs.gov/activity/latest/eq_01_02_28.html" TARGET=_blank>http://earthquake.usgs.gov/activity/latest/eq_01_02_28.html</A> <P>I'll bet my wife's sister in Portland felt this one!  I hope all you guys in Washington are OK.<BR>||||reg||1
