Z||000013||onfire||03-01-2001||01:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ur2biteme:<BR><B>onfire:<P>where in relation to Mt. Vernon do you live?  my sister lives there. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Federal Way is in between Seattle and Tacoma<P>About 20 miles south of Seattle and about 10 north of Tacoma.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tigger||03-01-2001||01:37 PM||||Good to hear everybody got throught it ok except for some minor injuries.<P>I had heard they found some fault lines after they imploded the King Dome.  Was this true, could it be the cause of the quake?||||reg||1
Z||000015||Coconut||03-01-2001||03:53 PM||||As it turns out, your friendly neighborhood Coconut and FieroGTgirl are okay! (One heck of a scare though!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) Thanks for the concern!<P>Boy, oh boy, was that one hell of a ride out here in Tacoma.  Me and a coworker were stacking a pallet of adhesives when it started. What was really strange about our encounter was that we heard a very loud roar thru the warehouse for a good 4 seconds. My first initial reaction was that it may have been one of the Air Force's C-141s coming in VERY LOW overhead (we aren't very far from McChord AFB.) A few more seconds and the shaking came, all I knew was I was not in the best place to be. In the middle of an aisle with racks of pallets overhead is not a very comforting thought when a building feels like it's having a spasm attack!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>I swear I had to have made a new world record in the 100 yd. dash and yelling "earthquake" on my way out!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Needless to say, I was the first one out of the building in no time flat. From outside the building, I actually saw our building swaying and trucks bouncing up and down, and the earth was just rolling under foot. Kinda made you feel a bit sea sick but what really got to me was the duration of this quake. The news reports said  30 to 45 seconds but man, it sure seemed like an eternity. All I could think about once I was outside the building was my wife and my parents.  She is in an office building and my folks are elderly. Talk about worry,I was going nuts thinking this may be the "BIG ONE" and not one of my loved ones around. Anyway, everything turned out okay, even my beloved GT came out unscathed!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Glad to hear everyone else came out good as well!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Did anyone up here feel any of the aftershocks?<P>Cruisin' (singing Stevie Ray Vaughn's 'If the House is a'Rockin')  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000016||ur2biteme||03-02-2001||01:43 AM||||it's been way too darn long since i've lived there.  i should have known that.  lol.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>aproaching 171k :)<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>a little piece of my madness</A>||||reg||1
Z||000017||hugh||03-02-2001||08:33 PM||||I heard on the radio this morning that the whole city of Seattle moved 5 millimeters.<BR>How the hell do they measure something like that?GPS?||||reg||1
Z||000018||gixxer||03-02-2001||08:49 PM||||Why,just run a plumb bob straight down from a geostationary satellite to the top of the Space Needle and........<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||theogre||03-03-2001||12:29 AM||||I know people in Olympia. scared the crap out of all of them. they were closer to it than Seatle. about 11 miles NNE and 35 down. Closer to the surface and this could have been a major $hitpile.<P>A few injuries down that way but nothing major aparantly. A number of buildings are F'd. Capitol Building is still being checked out last I knew. Some damage to the dome supporting structure.||||reg||1
Z||000020||onfire||03-03-2001||02:36 AM||||Nothing happened to the warehouse I work in, but the one across the street has alot of damage from what I hear.<P> It all started when their spinkler system went off. Then 2 sections of their roof caved in. Then the water main broke right next to them. Which the city is still trying to repair. The street is all tore up. ||||reg||1
